The legal text is the Constitution of the Republic of Serbia (Устав Републике Србије), as published in the
free official register of the Pravno-informacioni sistem of the Republic of Serbia (Службени гласник РС):

  Source: https://pravno-informacioni-sistem.rs, retrieved 29 October 2026.

Serbia's Law on Copyright and Related Rights (Закон о ауторском и сродним правима, "Службени гласник РС",
бр. 104/2009 and later amendments) does not treat laws, by-laws and other regulations as protected works.
This is a summary, not a quotation: the article number and exact wording were not checked against the
current official text when this repository was built.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph per
line; the text of articles is as the register prints it. The register's article captions, the headings of
parts and sections, the title block and the amendment notes ("*Службени гласник РС, број 115/2021 (Амандман I)")
were left out of the article files. The versions were arranged as git commits credited to the act that made
each change. The wording of the law was not changed.
The register does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
